rong> Lycoming County sells properties with delinquent taxes subject to existing liens and encumbrances.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Judicial Sale:</strong> The county holds the sale the year after the Upset Sale, selling properties free from all liens and offering investors a clean title.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p>All sales are final and conducted without guarantees or warranties, so performing thorough due diligence is crucial. Consult with an attorney and investigate properties thoroughly before participating in the auction.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-lycoming-county-s-tax-deed-sale-important-details\">Lycoming County&#8217;s Tax Deed Sale Important Details</h3>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"></figure>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full\"><picture><source srcset=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Lycoming-County-PA.webp 1081w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Lycoming-County-PA-541x360.webp 541w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Lycoming-County-PA-296x197.webp 296w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Lycoming-County-PA-768x512.webp 768w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Lycoming-County-PA-20x13.webp 20w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Lycoming-County-PA-32x21.webp 32w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1081px) 100vw, 1081px\" type=\"image/webp\"><img src=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Lycoming-County-PA.png\" height=\"720\" width=\"1081\" srcset=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Lycoming-County-PA.png 1081w, https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Lycoming-County-PA-541x360.png 541w, https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Lycoming-County-PA-296x197.png 296w, https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Lycoming-County-PA-768x512.png 768w, https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Lycoming-County-PA-20x13.png 20w, https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Lycoming-County-PA-32x21.png 32w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1081px) 100vw, 1081px\" class=\"wp-image-18525 sp-no-webp\" alt=\"Lycoming County PA\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"  > </picture></figure>\n</div>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons is-content-justification-center is-layout-flex wp-container-core-buttons-is-layout-16018d1d wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-button is-style-outline is-style-outline--1\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"https://linktr.ee/dustinhahnrealestateinvesting\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Click Here to Book a Call with Dustin Hahn</a></div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:30px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"Pro-Tips-for-Bidders\">Pro Tips for Bidders</h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Research Local Laws</strong>: Understand the legal framework in Lycoming County.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Visit the Local Treasurer’s Website</strong>: Stay updated with the latest tax sale information.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Check the Auction Site</strong>: Review property listings, as they can change up until the sale date.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Consult an Attorney</strong>: Ensure all legal aspects are covered before making a bid.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"Useful-Links\">For More Details:</h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><a href=\"https://www.lyco.org/Departments/Tax-Claim-Bureau/Tax-Sales\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">Lycoming County Tax Sale Information</mark></a></li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https://www.lyco.org/Departments/Collections-Office-Tax-Claim-Bureau\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">Lycoming County Auction Site Information</mark></a></li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https://www.lyco.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">General County Information</mark></a></li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"Frequently-Asked-Questions\">Frequently Asked Questions</h4>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>How can I participate in the Lycoming County Tax Sale?</strong><br><strong>A1:</strong> To participate, You must pre-register with the Tax Claim Bureau and follow all registration instructions.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>What types of properties are available at the tax sales?</strong><br><strong>A:</strong> Tax sales in Lycoming County offer various properties, including residential, commercial, and vacant land, all sold at a fraction of their market value.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>What payment methods are accepted at the Lycoming County Tax Sale?</strong><br><strong>A:</strong> Payments for properties purchased at the auction can typically be made via cash, certified check, or money order. Make sure to check the county&#8217;s official guidelines for exact payment instructions.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Are there any risks involved in purchasing properties at the tax sale?</strong><br><strong>A:</strong> Yes, investing in tax sales involves risks such as potential existing liens, encumbrances, or property condition issues. Always perform due diligence and consult with an attorney before bidding.</p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"Need-a-Hand?\">Need a Hand?</h4>\n\n\n\n<p>We’re here to help with any questions or guidance you may need regarding tax lien and deed investing. Feel free to reach out and book a consultation or access our free resources for more detailed advice on navigating tax sales. <a href=\"https://linktr.ee/dustinha